{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetJFcc6pm6ibxM1JRMEc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, here are my findings:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that transitions a shipment from `CREATED` to `CONFIRMED`, succeeds idempotently on already-confirmed shipments, and rejects cancelled or non-existent shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model with status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED): `Shipment.kt:9-27`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository with CRUD operations: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`\n- ShipmentController with create/read/list endpoints: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- ApiException hierarchy (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException): `ApiExceptions.kt:11-24`\n- Error codes enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS: `ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler for centralized error response formatting: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28`\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler serializes them to ApiError envelope\n- ResourceNotFoundException → 404 with ErrorCode\n- ConflictException → 409 with ErrorCode\n- Tests assert on response bodies (error.code, error.message), not just status codes\n- Tests use separate GET requests after state changes to verify persistence (per the testing-and-verification skill)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add new ErrorCode for invalid state transitions (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests covering all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotent retry not properly tested (test pattern requires separate GET after the repeated call)\n- Persistence not verified through endpoint GET (if tested only via response body)\n- New error code might be overlooked\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket fully specifies all four cases and their responses.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to ErrorCode enum. This error code will be thrown when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment, which violates the state machine.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a `confirm` method:\n   - Route: `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Logic: \n     - Find the shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing\n     - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED and save\n     - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n     - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n     - Return the (possibly unchanged) shipment with HTTP 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four tests:\n   - Test 1: Confirm a CREATED shipment → 200, response body has CONFIRMED status, then verify via separate GET\n   - Test 2: Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → 200, unchanged (idempotent), call again to verify repeat succeeds\n   - Test 3: Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code, verify via separate GET that state is unchanged\n   - Test 4: Confirm a non-existent shipment → 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected:** I considered putting the confirm logic in a separate service layer (ShipmentService), but rejected it because:\n- The existing codebase has no service layer (OrderController works directly with OrderRepository)\n- The confirm logic is simple (no orchestration across multiple repositories)\n- Adding a service would be unrelated refactoring outside the necessary set of changes\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Repository operation | Response status | Response body | ErrorCode |\n|------|-------|----------------------|-----------------|---------------|-----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId | update status to CONFIRMED, save | 200 | Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | N/A |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | shipmentId | none (found, no change) | 200 | Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | N/A |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId | none (found, reject) | 409 | ApiError(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) | SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE |\n| Confirm not found | shipmentId | none (not found) | 404 | ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirms a created shipment and persists it` — POST confirm on CREATED → 200, assert response body has CONFIRMED, then GET to verify persisted state\n2. `idempotent confirm succeeds twice` — POST confirm twice on same shipment → first is 200 with CONFIRMED, second is also 200 with same body\n3. `refuses to confirm a cancelled shipment with error code` — Write CANCELLED shipment to repo, POST confirm → 409, assert `error.code` = SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, then GET to verify unchanged\n4. `returns 404 for unknown shipment` — POST confirm on non-existent ID → 404, assert `error.code` = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":769,"cache_read_input_tokens":22074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":769},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519f4470-36b2-4739-aa56-77a55f150b96","uuid":"6a4ba461-265e-4cc3-91df-cfe782e0e346","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:57:48.343Z","request_id":"req_011CetJFboizdAsJoWbkXjJ1"}
