{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetJKyK9incMYbjGPQSrS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests passed. The verification command succeeded:\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** \n- 17 tests run total\n- 0 failures\n- 0 errors\n- BUILD SUCCESS\n- ShipmentControllerTest specifically shows 9 tests passing (5 original + 4 new confirm tests)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — The BUILD SUCCESS with all 17 tests passing confirms this.\n\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 OrderControllerTest tests, 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests, and 3 CustomerControllerTest tests pass without modification.\n\n3. ✅ **`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test `confirms a created shipment and persists it` creates a CREATED shipment, calls the endpoint, asserts the response body has CONFIRMED status, then makes a separate GET request to verify persistence.\n\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — The new `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code follows the existing pattern. ConflictException for 409 and ResourceNotFoundException for 404 are used consistently with OrderController. GlobalExceptionHandler converts these to the ApiError envelope automatically.\n\n5. ✅ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused**:\n   - Test `idempotent confirm succeeds when shipment is already confirmed` confirms twice and verifies both succeed with 200.\n   - Test `refuses to confirm a cancelled shipment with error code` sets up a CANCELLED shipment and asserts 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code, then verifies via GET the state is unchanged.\n   - Test `returns 404 for confirming an unknown shipment` calls confirm on non-existent shipment and asserts 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code.\n\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No changes to pom.xml; only Kotlin/Spring standard features used.\n\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only three production files modified:\n   - `ApiError.kt` — added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code (necessary)\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` — added confirm endpoint (necessary)\n   - `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — added tests (necessary)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added single line to ErrorCode enum. Necessary because the ticket requires rejecting cancelled shipments with a distinct error code (409 with a code value).\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added 17-line `confirm` method and updated class docstring. The confirm method:\n  - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if shipment doesn't exist (404 case)\n  - Throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE if cancelled (409 case)\n  - Updates status to CONFIRMED only if currently CREATED\n  - Returns unchanged shipment if already CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n  - Uses `copy()` to immutably create updated shipment (Kotlin data class pattern)\n  - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() for 200 success (different from create's 201 by design)\n  \n  This had to change per ticket requirement.\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 4 new test methods (49 lines added). Each test:\n  - Tests a distinct case from the ticket requirements\n  - Asserts on response bodies (not just status codes)\n  - Uses separate GET requests after state changes to verify persistence\n  - Uses separate GET requests after refused calls to verify no state change\n  - Asserts error codes in error responses (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n  \n  These had to be added per acceptance criteria #5.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests pass, no unrelated files changed.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement\n: Add a POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED, succeeds idempotently on already-confirmed shipments, and rejects cancelled or non-existent shipments.\n\nChanged\n: ApiError.kt — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for invalid state transitions (necessary for 409 response to cancelled shipment confirmation).\n: ShipmentController.kt — Added confirm endpoint that handles state transitions (CREATED→CONFIRMED, CONFIRMED→idempotent no-change, CANCELLED→409, not found→404).\n: ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added four new tests covering confirm-created, idempotent-confirm, refuse-cancelled, and not-found cases, each verifying state through separate GET requests.\n\nTests\n: `confirms a created shipment and persists it` — Verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition persists via separate GET.\n: `idempotent confirm succeeds when shipment is already confirmed` — Confirms twice, verifies second call also succeeds with same response.\n: `refuses to confirm a cancelled shipment with error code` — Sets up CANCELLED state, asserts 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code, verifies GET shows state unchanged.\n: `returns 404 for confirming an unknown shipment` — Asserts 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code.\n\nVerification\n: Command: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n: Result: 17 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS. ShipmentControllerTest shows 9 tests passing (5 original + 4 new).\n\nNot done\n: Nothing. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests pass, verification command succeeded."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3320,"cache_read_input_tokens":29042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3320},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"519f4470-36b2-4739-aa56-77a55f150b96","uuid":"1c079ca1-dc8a-43d8-b415-aa4a7f58fddc","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:58:46.856Z","request_id":"req_0